#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The 96 HUD glyph shapes, ASCII 32..127, as 8x8 ASCII art.

Data only. make_hud_tiles.py turns these into actual SNES tiles -- once with a
drop shadow for body text, once on an opaque plate for the chyron, and once at
2x with an outline for display type.

Each glyph is 7 wide and 7 tall inside an 8x8 cell: column 7 is empty in every
glyph and no capital uses row 7, which is what leaves room for a 1px shadow
offset down and right. Lowercase descenders (g j p q y , ; _) do use row 7, so
their shadow is clipped -- UI copy is uppercase, so it never shows.

G, Q and R were redrawn from the original font to keep their tails out of row
7. Without that they were the only capitals that could not carry a shadow.
"""

